WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
Shine a lamp on a sheet of white paper.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.240
The lit patch can be seen
from anywhere in the room.

3
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.930
Now aim a laser at a smooth, flat mirror.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.240
Three observers stand nearby.

5
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.190
Only one of them receives
the reflected beam.

6
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:21.180
So why can everyone see the paper, but
only one spot sees the mirror's reflection?

7
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.900
In this mission, you'll draw ray diagrams,

8
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.980
with arrows running from
the source, to the surface,

9
00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.290
to the eye.

10
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.010
Then you'll find out
when the ray model works,

11
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.790
and when it fails.

12
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.230
Your mission: explain why
everyone can see the paper,

13
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.390
but only one spot sees
the laser's reflection.
